                <pb facs="0328" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg220"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/163: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-12T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1927—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 12—8:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>547. Following from American consul at Nanking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 11, 8 p.m. A considerable number of American mission buildings in
                            Nanking are still occupied as barracks, and one church is being used as
                            a military hospital.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
